    "visibility" "2"
    "title" "First Person"
    "description" "[h1]First Person[/h1]
Stand on your own factory floor and watch the shapes go past at eye level.

New game, Regular, [b]First Person[/b]. You arrive at the vortex one and a half tiles tall, with your factory around you instead of below you, and you stay there - this is a scenario rather than a camera toggle. Resources are closer and more generous than usual, because everything here is a walk.

[h2]What you can do down there[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Walk[/b] your platforms, with gravity, walls and step-up. Machines are steps rather than walls, so a covered platform is somewhere you can cross.
[*][b]Fall off the edge[/b] - and be put back on the last solid ground, because a space platform has edges and there is nothing under them.
[*][b]Build[/b] at a crosshair. Placing, deleting and the pipette all work on whatever you are looking at.
[*][b]Ride the belts.[/b] Stand on one and it carries you, at the speed it really moves - research upgrades included.
[*][b]Ride the trains.[/b] Hold the board key while one is in your crosshair and you climb onto the engine, across platforms, up lifts, over the jumps between them and around onto the underside of an inverted track.
[*][b]Fly[/b], once you have researched it, and fast travel between the waypoints you have already placed.
[/list]

[h2]Controls[/h2]
Every key is rebindable in the game's own settings, under [b]First Person[/b]. Out of the box:
[list]
[*][b]Your movement keys[/b] - walk. It uses your bindings, not hardcoded WASD.
[*][b]Your move-faster key[/b] - sprint, on foot and in the air.
[*][b]Space[/b] - jump. Double-tap to fly.
[*][b]Tab[/b] (hold) - release the mouse for the HUD, the side panels and the menus.
[*][b]F5[/b] - travel to your next waypoint. Clicking one on the map, or the home icon, travels there too.
[*][b]F[/b] (hold) - board the train in your crosshair. It stands aside for mirror while you are holding a building.
[*][b]Q[/b] and [b]E[/b] - the build layer, as always. While flying it is yours to pick rather than following your altitude.
[*][b]Wheel[/b] - move through the toolbar. Ctrl and the wheel steps into a submenu and back out.
[/list]

[h2]Three things are researched[/h2]
Walking and building are free. [b]Jet Pack[/b], [b]Waypoint Travel[/b] and [b]Train Riding[/b] are nodes in a First Person research category, priced against the top of the vanilla ladder, so the scenario opens up as you play rather than arriving complete. Flight is deliberately no faster than a train until you sprint.

[h2]For other mod authors[/h2]
This is meant to be built on. One static class, [b]FirstPersonControl[/b], lets another mod lock the player into first person in any save, turn the scenario off, switch any of the three features off or make them free, set their prices, or change the walking and flight speeds. Reference the dll or drive it reflectively - it is plain static fields either way.

[h2]Before you install[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]It does not affect save games.[/b] Add it to an existing save or remove it from one; nothing in an ordinary save changes, because first person only happens in its own scenario.
[*]Restart the game after installing - the scenario and the research nodes are game data, so a hot reload will not add them.
[*]Requires Shapez Shifter and MonoMod.RuntimeDetour.
[/list]

Bugs and requests: https://github.com/QuinnBast/Shapez2-Mods/issues
Licensed under Apache 2.0."
}
